---
toolSlug: agent-security-audit
permalink: /tools/agent-security-audit/
---

<div class="tool-group">
  <label for="asa-input">Paste your AI agent configuration</label>
  <textarea id="asa-input" rows="16" placeholder='Paste MCP server definitions, OpenAI function calling schemas, Anthropic tool definitions, raw tool lists, or agent system prompts with tool access.&#10;&#10;Examples:&#10;  { "mcpServers": { "filesystem": { ... } } }&#10;  { "tools": [{ "type": "function", "function": { ... } }] }&#10;  { "tools": [{ "name": "...", "input_schema": { ... } }] }' spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off"></textarea>
</div>

<div class="tool-row">
  <button class="btn btn--primary" id="asa-audit-btn">Audit</button>
  <button class="btn" id="asa-example-btn">Try Example</button>
  <button class="btn" id="asa-clear-btn">Clear</button>
  <div id="asa-summary" style="margin-left:auto;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--text-3,#888);align-self:center;"></div>
</div>

<p style="font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--text-3,#888);line-height:1.55;">Static heuristic review only. Capabilities are inferred from names, descriptions, and configuration shapes; the page does not inspect an MCP server's implementation, sandbox, approval flow, or runtime enforcement, and it does not prove exploitability.</p>

<div id="asa-results" style="display:none;">
  <div id="asa-score-section"></div>
  <div id="asa-findings"></div>
  <div id="asa-paths"></div>
  <div id="asa-recommendations"></div>
</div>

<div id="asa-empty" class="asa-empty-msg">Paste an agent configuration above and click "Audit".</div>

